      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "ID verification= 101 ways to kill a game. Yeah. No thanks. I'd literally delete all my content and remove my account if that happened.\nAge related safety systems require a way to verify the age of a user otherwise they would be easily abused and have no value or provide no solution. \nTools already exist in the game to deal with this. Reporting with an actual moderation ticket and proof, as well as blocking a user. \nIn order to set age related safety, all users would have to provide a government issued ID which can also be used. As kids could and would just use their parents ID. \nAge related safety is simply not possible without verification of age. \nThis would directly impact all users while not providing a solution to the issue and would directly impact the viability of the platform. It doesn't seem like a viable solution at all. \nEducation should be at the forefront of anyone's mind who wishes to prevent this form of issue. Using already existing tools and educating young teens so they are aware of the dangers of the world and virtually all internet platforms is important and may fall mostly on the shoulders of the peers of the young teen. \nAs there is simply no way to have age related safety setting without verification of age, this canny is unviable. Not saying methods shouldn't be considered, I've listed some myself and the game already has viable tools, but this canny as written isn't viable.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
