      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f99a97e4d4afb3fb6674ca5|full_name}: Facebook, Steam already requires DoB (Date of Birth) to be entered to create an account, this would be hilariously easy to implement. You'd be better off acknowledging that kids who are truthful when creating an account would be much better off not seeing content and interacting with people which violate section 12d of the VRChat TOS.\nAll you have to do is link a Steam account or make an Oculus account and content filters would be put in place in the background, avatars marked as obscene or that contain gore could simply show up as errors for these users.\nQuest accounts could simply be restricted from seeing all obscene-labelled content given the age-distribution of their user-base.\nVRChat already has it so visitors who enter through the tutorial meet up with other visitors after they go through one of the portals, it would be easy to just make it to where they pair-up in instances with the most visitors and new trust ranks for a few hours.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
